The oldest River, wide and ancient, decided to stop flowing. "I will keep my waters for myself," she declared. Her current slowed to stillness, and her banks turned to mud.

But then a strange thing happened. Without movement, the River began to stagnate. Fish died, plants withered, and the water turned foul. The River, in her stillness, was dying.

