The River understood then: she had never been losing her water—she had been sending it on a journey. Every drop that reached the Sea returned transformed as rain, bringing news from the mountaintops and nourishment from the clouds.

From that day, the River flowed freely again, knowing that generosity creates not loss but circulation—an endless cycle where giving and receiving are one continuous motion.

